From 4513eef83627ddbbf4d296ab38bb466d0a58d37d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JU <jusamuel@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:43:23 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] feat(collect): protocol/data-tag sync API, init routine,
 command gap, frame start (C4)

Server (read-only, no DB change)
- GET /api/core/sync/protocols[/{ptlGrpCd}], GET /api/core/sync/data-tags?devCd= (client key chain)
- Response {revision (content SHA-256), items, removed}; groups -> protocols -> packets, data tags by device

Desktop
- Sync models + JuProviderApiClient.GetProtocolGroupsAsync / GetDataTagsAsync
- CollectionProfile (per protocol group, desktop resource until DB columns): frame rule, command gap,
  init routine, protocol overlays; built-in GTEC (STOP -> check -> sensor info -> mode, 200 ms gap, '{' start)
- CollectionPlanBuilder: server definitions + profile -> DeviceSession config, TAG_ID=CH<n> mapping
- DeviceSession: init routine on connect/reconnect (Initializing state, external commands wait)
- Frame rule start option: drop noise before start, drop broken frame when next start arrives before end
- Tests: frame start/noise, profile/plan, init routine, gap, reconnect regression on GTEC-like device; server service test

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
